7	 signed service request matching the manifest. Such sources must use the separate
8	 legacy import/salvage workflows; no synthetic historical admission is minted.
9	+
10	+### Final review decisions for the first profile-3 storage slice
11	+
12	+Fresh actual Opus 5.5 at 8244375 approved destination implementation readiness
13	+with follow-ups; the unmodified report is preserved in
14	+`.design/reviews/kan-v2-copy-planner-opus/`. These decisions resolve C-F1, C-F3
15	+and C-F4 before any profile-3 destination write. They are implementation
16	+requirements, not claims that the destination runtime exists.
17	+
18	+**One meaning of copied history (C-F1).** Profile 2 is admitted-only. Its audit,
19	+writable opener, verification, backup and rebuild must refuse retained-verified
20	+proofs. Profile 3 is the only recipe-1 copy target and the only profile permitted
21	+to contain a retained-verified prefix. RetryImported targets profile 3 only.
22	+This supersedes the earlier profile-2 allowance for a plan-less upgrade prefix
23	+and its synthetic acceptance fixture. No production profile-2 archive has been
24	+provisioned in this work; there is no silent conversion or deletion. Any existing
25	+experimental file refused by the stricter rule stays untouched. The next storage
26	+slice must implement and independently review this distinction before writing a
27	+profile-3 destination.
28	+
29	+**Original membership and deduplication (C-F3).** An original object's CID remains
30	+in upgrade_objects permanently even if a later current-issuer admission uses the
31	+same CID. There is one content-addressed payload, with both original membership
32	+and later occurrence lineage. Audits allow shared CIDs; they never subtract or
33	+re-attribute original membership. No foreign-key cascade may destroy inventory
34	+metadata when a payload becomes unavailable.
35	+
36	+**Explicit profile selection and takeover (C-F4).** Owner APIs select profile 3 by
37	+its distinct type; owner CLI lifecycle commands require explicit profile 3 along
38	+with archive/scope/issuer pins. Existing all-or-none pins continue to mean profile
39	+2 unless the new profile option is supplied. No user_version auto-detection
40	+selects trust. Create/resume additionally require the retained exact plan artifact
41	+and external archive pin. Verify/backup/rebuild may read the stored plan only to
42	+check it against the explicit configured profile and pins.
43	+
44	+Takeover means the owner stops or fences the old admitting service and configures
45	+one replacement as the sole write destination. Copy, backup, verify and rebuild
46	+never perform that activation or claim to establish cross-host fencing. Their
47	+outputs remain unpromoted. The later service/admin integration must expose the
48	+explicit activation workflow; an ordinary backup is not an independent archive.
49	+The owner-side API assumes its signer/grants come from that trusted configuration.
50	+
51	+**Bundle boundary remains a separate required checkpoint (C-F2).** Before any
52	+bundle writer exists, define an encapsulation/publication format that cannot be
53	+selected as a standalone archive member through the product's ordinary writable
54	+configuration. Filling missing blobs inside a bundle must not bypass the retained
55	+observation/resolution history. A privileged owner manually extracting bytes is
56	+outside that product boundary, not something local locks can prevent.
57	+Resolution preserves source-copy completeness independently of payload completeness:
58	+a payload-complete but unfinished profile-3 copy remains unfinished and cannot
59	+admit. Publishing it does not finish migration or authorize a second writer.
60	+Physical encoding, atomic publication and activation tests remain open for the
61	+bundle-specific design review; the copy-only schema approval does not close them.
